{"seconds": 90.2, "exit": 0, "final": "After Black's forced Rxd8, White is up a queen (and pawn) for rook and bishop\u2014a decisive material advantage. \n\n---\n\n**Coaching note:**\n\nThe knight fork to e6 is the key blow. It attacks both the queen and g7-pawn, forcing Black into 1...Bxc3+ (the only try to create counterplay). After 2. Qxc3, Black recaptures the knight with 2...Bxe6, but then 3. Rxd8+ wins the queen outright. The lesson: when your opponent's pieces are loosely coordinated, look for well-placed knight jumps that create multiple threats. Even if they're attacked, they often lead to forcing sequences that win material.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nxe6\", \"line\": [\"Nxe6\", \"Bxc3+\", \"Qxc3\", \"Bxe6\", \"Rxd8+\", \"Rxd8\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12", "move": "Qh5+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1pn2/1p6/1bpNPB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 4 12", "move": "Nxe6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1Nn2/1p6/1bp1PB2/2N2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R b Kkq - 0 12", "move": "Bxc3+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1Nn2/1p6/2p1PB2/2b2Q2/PP3PPP/3RKB1R w Kkq - 0 13", "move": "Qxc3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2pb2pp/p1n1Nn2/1p6/2p1PB2/2Q5/PP3PPP/3RKB1R b Kkq - 0 13", "move": "Bxe6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qk2r/2p3pp/p1n1bn2/1p6/2p1PB2/2Q5/PP3PPP